+Config (`.env`): `HOSTINGER_API`, `PF_VPS_ID`, `PF_DOMAIN`, `PF_PROJECT`, `PF_GIT_URL`, `PF_GIT_REF`, `TELESCOPE_ENABLED`, `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`, `DISCORD_MENTION_ID`, `LOG_STACK`, `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`.
 
 ## Discord ops alerts
 
@@ -68,6 +68,8 @@ ## Discord ops alerts
 | --- | --- |
 | Env | `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` → `config('services.discord.webhook_url')` |
 | Client | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context = [])` |
+| Mention | `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` → `config('services.discord.mention_id')`; a Discord user ID (17–20 digits, surrounding whitespace trimmed). Every alert ends with `<@ID>` on its own line so it pings that user. Empty or invalid (`@everyone`, `123`, multi-line values, …) → no mention |
+| Length | Limit is 1800 characters for the whole content; the mention is reserved room and never truncated, the title/message/context are truncated instead |
 | Unconfigured | Empty/missing URL → silent no-op (safe for CI) |
 | Failures | Non-2xx / transport errors are logged without the webhook URL; they do not throw |
 
